[2026-03-14T22:24:37.646Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R3cYH12aBk7UfNMwb1vSXM","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Skill File\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Replay CLI tool enables users to record application sessions, gather performance data, and debug issues. It supports installation via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun.\n\n## Key Features\n\n**Authentication:** Users generate an API key from https://app.replay.io settings and store it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n**Core Commands:**\n- `record [url]` - Launches the Replay Browser to capture a session\n- `upload [ids...]` - Uploads recordings with optional interactive selection\n- `list` - Displays local recordings with metadata\n- `remove [ids...]` - Deletes recordings locally\n- `login/logout` - Manages account access\n- `info` - Shows CLI and browser version details\n\n**Advanced Features:**\n- Source map uploading for debugging\n- Interactive menus when no arguments provided\n- JSON output option for programmatic access\n- Automatic update checking\n\n## Integration\n\nThe tool integrates with Claude through an MCP server, allowing users to debug recorded applications by running the Replay MCP Server with their `REPLAY_API_KEY` authorization header.\n\n## Workflow\n\nTypical usage: record a session → upload automatically or manually → access the recording URL for analysis and debugging."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"630917b2-6ea2-4867-b126-d32adb3e5b74","uuid":"327fa443-7ef5-43d1-88b7-b4379ebeba16","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Skill File\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Replay CLI tool enables users to record application sessions, gather performance data, and debug issues. It supports installation via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun.\n\n## Key Features\n\n**Authentication:** Users generate an API key from https://app.replay.io settings and store it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n**Core Commands:**\n- `record [url]` - Launches the Replay Browser to capture a session\n- `upload [ids...]` - Uploads recordings with optional interactive selection\n- `list` - Displays local recordings with metadata\n- `remove [ids...]` - Deletes recordings locally\n- `login/logout` - Manages account access\n- `info` - Shows CLI and browser version details\n\n**Advanced Features:**\n- Source map uploading for debugging\n- Interactive menus when no arguments provided\n- JSON output option for programmatic access\n- Automatic update checking\n\n## Integration\n\nThe tool integrates with Claude through an MCP server, allowing users to debug recorded applications by running the Replay MCP Server with their `REPLAY_API_KEY` authorization header.\n\n## Workflow\n\nTypical usage: record a session → upload automatically or manually → access the recording URL for analysis and debugging.","durationMs":3636,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-14T22:24:38.359Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CAAifTV2KosSCnyZW4GyV6","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Skill File Content\n\n**Name:** replay-mcp\n\n**Description:** Tool for inspecting https://replay.io recordings to investigate web app behavior.\n\n**Key Capabilities:**\n\nThe skill provides exploratory and explanatory tools for analyzing recordings:\n\n- **Exploratory Tools:** Identify errors, timeline events (console messages, network requests, React renders), and source code execution\n- **Explanatory Tools:** Understand causality through stack traces, control dependencies, point descriptions, element inspection, and expression evaluation\n\n**Core Concept:** \"The recording is essentially a gigantic database containing everything that happened while the app executed,\" with investigations framed around specific questions answered through systematic exploration and hypothesis validation.\n\n**Methodology:** The documentation recommends a structured approach: formulate questions, use exploratory tools to identify relevant events, employ explanatory tools to understand causality, develop hypotheses supported by gathered data, and explain conclusions with evidence.\n\n**Notable Tools Include:**\n- ListSources, ReadSource, SearchSources (code analysis)\n- ConsoleMessages, NetworkRequest, ReactRenders (event tracking)\n- Logpoint (expression monitoring across execution)\n- ControlDependency (event causality analysis)\n\nThe skill emphasizes avoiding premature conclusions and leveraging the recording's complete execution data for precise investigation."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"630917b2-6ea2-4867-b126-d32adb3e5b74","uuid":"a10ac962-68e7-48a2-ac18-d1a70f9a14c6","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Skill File Content\n\n**Name:** replay-mcp\n\n**Description:** Tool for inspecting https://replay.io recordings to investigate web app behavior.\n\n**Key Capabilities:**\n\nThe skill provides exploratory and explanatory tools for analyzing recordings:\n\n- **Exploratory Tools:** Identify errors, timeline events (console messages, network requests, React renders), and source code execution\n- **Explanatory Tools:** Understand causality through stack traces, control dependencies, point descriptions, element inspection, and expression evaluation\n\n**Core Concept:** \"The recording is essentially a gigantic database containing everything that happened while the app executed,\" with investigations framed around specific questions answered through systematic exploration and hypothesis validation.\n\n**Methodology:** The documentation recommends a structured approach: formulate questions, use exploratory tools to identify relevant events, employ explanatory tools to understand causality, develop hypotheses supported by gathered data, and explain conclusions with evidence.\n\n**Notable Tools Include:**\n- ListSources, ReadSource, SearchSources (code analysis)\n- ConsoleMessages, NetworkRequest, ReactRenders (event tracking)\n- Logpoint (expression monitoring across execution)\n- ControlDependency (event causality analysis)\n\nThe skill emphasizes avoiding premature conclusions and leveraging the recording's complete execution data for precise investigation.","durationMs":3458,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
